== (b) gate network R911+R912 / R921+R922 = 2 x 200 ohm 1206 (UNI-ROYAL C18002) in series
PASS  opto-triac surge limit: R = VPK / ITSM: minimum 357.8 ohm; fitted 400 ohm (-1% = 396): peak 0.904 A <= 1 A (x1.11); the rating is a single 60 Hz cycle, so it bounds a longer pulse than the 100 us the Lite-On sheet gave
PASS  gate drive reaches IGT: line voltage that drives IGT max through 404 ohm = 24.5 V (4.6 deg after the crossing at 216 V rms); the opto fires below 20 V, its gate current then keeps rising with the line (the opto stays latched, IH typ 0.5 mA); peak gate current 0.90 A <= IGM 4 A (x4.4)
NOTE  1206 voltage rating of a 200 ohm part (UNI-ROYAL V.3 p.5, amended 2026-11-18, finding 4.2): RCWV = sqrt(0.25 W x 200 ohm) = 7.07 V; overload voltage 2.5 x RCWV = 17.7 V (the 200 V and 400 V figures are maxima, not the rating); dielectric 500 V; no pulse rating stated
NOTE  firing: 10.1 V per resistor at IGT 50 mA = x1.43 of RCWV and 0.57 of the overload voltage, for the ramp below; surge case (false trigger at the line peak): 178.9 V per resistor = x25.3 of RCWV and x10.1 of the overload voltage: NOT within the resistor's rating; the pulse capability is unsourced (basis: onsemi Fig. 12 p.7, the main board's identical network, rare and fail-safe)
NOTE  surge case power in each resistor: 0.904 A x 178.9 V = 162 W (x647 of the 250 mW rating) until the triac latches (microseconds, unsourced): 162 uJ per us, 1.6 mJ at 10 us, 16.2 mJ at 100 us (durations assumed); with the 775 V clamp across the pair: 1.96 A, 387.5 V and 758 W each
   power: during the firing ramp each resistor passes at most IGT 50 mA: 0.505 W for the ramp from the opto's turn-on (<= 20 V) to the triac's latch (24.5 V), (24.5 - 20) V at the line's slope 2 pi f VPK = 112 V/ms gives 0.040 ms, 2.02 mW average at 100 firings a second (250 mW rated; the share 0.6 gives 150 mW)
PASS  triac latches at firing: main current at the firing point at least 24.5 V / 52.7 ohm (the element's top resistance) = 0.46 A against IL 70 mA max (x6.6)
   gate-to-MT1 short fault (a shorted triac gate): 0.62 A rms through the 400 ohm, peak 0.89 A, 156 W in the two resistors: they open; the heater stays off (fails off); the opto-triac's 1 A is a single-cycle rating and the time the resistors take to open is not sourced

