   the 800 V test voltage of IDRM1 is above the 357.8 V peak the leakage sees on this board: no credit is taken for that
   IDRM2 2 mA flows only while the LED is on and the line is above the inhibit voltage (the commanded state): it is not a hold-off figure. Against the minimum trigger current 2.5 mA it is x1.25; across 404 ohm it is 0.81 V. So a command that starts mid-half-cycle could fire before the next zero: a non-zero-cross turn-on, no hazard (the heater was commanded on)
   LED current in reset / unpowered: at most 5 uA (main board row), 1000 times under IFT max 5 mA; cable loose: +5V_WB or HEAT_x_LED_K open gives 0 A

